---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Testimonials preview | Saielle DaSilva"
  description="Three double-border testimonial card designs with blue accents."
>
  <style>
    :root {
      --acc-blue: #4f7ea8;
    }

    .preview-head {
      padding-block: var(--space-8) var(--space-5);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .preview-head h1 {
      max-width: none;
      font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
    }
    .preview-panel {
      padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 5.5rem);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .preview-panel .panel-label {
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.25em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    }
    .preview-panel h2 {
      font-size: 1.7rem;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-7);
    }

    /* Shared card shell: double border like .rate-card / .contact-card */
    .tcard {
      position: relative;
      border: 1px solid var(--ink);
      background: var(--paper);
      padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-7);
    }
    .tcard::after {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      inset: 3px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      pointer-events: none;
    }
    .tcard .q {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-optical-sizing: auto;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    }
    .tcard .a {
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin: 0;
    }

    /* ---- New A: blue top keyline ---- */
    .ta-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
      gap: var(--space-5);
    }
    .ta-card::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      right: 0;
      height: 4px;
      background: var(--acc-blue);
      z-index: 1;
    }

    /* ---- New B: blue left rule + attribution keyline ---- */
    .tb-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
      gap: var(--space-5);
    }
    .tb-card {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
    }
    .tb-card::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      top: var(--space-6);
      bottom: var(--space-6);
      left: 0;
      width: 4px;
      background: var(--acc-blue);
    }
    .tb-card .q {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
    }
    .tb-attrib {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      padding-top: var(--space-4);
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: var(--space-3);
    }
    .tb-attrib .a {
      margin: 0;
    }
    .tb-attrib .idx {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-style: italic;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--acc-blue);
    }

    /* ---- New C: big blue index numeral ---- */
    .tc-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
      gap: var(--space-5);
    }
    .tc-card {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
    }
    .tc-card .num {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: 3rem;
      line-height: 1;
      color: var(--acc-blue);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
    }
    .tc-card .q {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
    }
    .tc-card .a {
      margin-top: auto;
    }
  </style>

  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head preview-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Testimonials · iteration 3</p>
      <h1>Double-border cards, blue keylines.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        No photos. Visual interest from blue accents, keylines and index
        numerals. Same double border as the rates and contact form.
      </p>
    </header>
  </section>

  <!-- New A -->
  <section class="preview-panel" aria-label="Option A blue top keyline">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="panel-label">A · Blue top keyline</p>
      <div class="ta-grid">
        <div class="tcard ta-card">
          <p class="q">
            Saielle doesn't tell you what you want to hear. She names the
            decision you've been avoiding and gives you the frame to make it,
            then she stays until it lands.
          </p>
          <p class="a">Chief Product Officer · UK scale-up</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tcard ta-card">
          <p class="q">
            She gave our talk on higher impact product decisions, and the room
            hasn't made the same misaligned choice since. Teams that had never
            questioned the plan started asking which one thing mattered most.
          </p>
          <p class="a">Product leader · Sainsbury's</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tcard ta-card">
          <p class="q">
            The rare leader who can go from a whiteboard strategy to shipped
            code in the same week. She brought our AI story into focus when
            nobody else could.
          </p>
          <p class="a">Founder &amp; CEO · pre-seed AI startup</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- New B -->
  <section class="preview-panel" aria-label="Option B blue left rule">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="panel-label">B · Blue left rule + divider</p>
      <div class="tb-grid">
        <div class="tcard tb-card">
          <p class="q">
            Saielle doesn't tell you what you want to hear. She names the
            decision you've been avoiding and gives you the frame to make it,
            then she stays until it lands.
          </p>
          <div class="tb-attrib">
            <p class="a">Chief Product Officer · UK scale-up</p>
            <span class="idx">01</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tcard tb-card">
          <p class="q">
            She gave our talk on higher impact product decisions, and the room
            hasn't made the same misaligned choice since. Teams that had never
            questioned the plan started asking which one thing mattered most.
          </p>
          <div class="tb-attrib">
            <p class="a">Product leader · Sainsbury's</p>
            <span class="idx">02</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tcard tb-card">
          <p class="q">
            The rare leader who can go from a whiteboard strategy to shipped
            code in the same week. She brought our AI story into focus when
            nobody else could.
          </p>
          <div class="tb-attrib">
            <p class="a">Founder &amp; CEO · pre-seed AI startup</p>
            <span class="idx">03</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- New C -->
  <section class="preview-panel" aria-label="Option C big index numeral">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="panel-label">C · Large blue index numeral</p>
      <div class="tc-grid">
        <div class="tcard tc-card">
          <span class="num">01</span>
          <p class="q">
            Saielle doesn't tell you what you want to hear. She names the
            decision you've been avoiding and gives you the frame to make it,
            then she stays until it lands.
          </p>
          <p class="a">Chief Product Officer · UK scale-up</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tcard tc-card">
          <span class="num">02</span>
          <p class="q">
            She gave our talk on higher impact product decisions, and the room
            hasn't made the same misaligned choice since. Teams that had never
            questioned the plan started asking which one thing mattered most.
          </p>
          <p class="a">Product leader · Sainsbury's</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tcard tc-card">
          <span class="num">03</span>
          <p class="q">
            The rare leader who can go from a whiteboard strategy to shipped
            code in the same week. She brought our AI story into focus when
            nobody else could.
          </p>
          <p class="a">Founder &amp; CEO · pre-seed AI startup</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
